{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"3182","artifact_type":"architect","name":"plan/architect-backlog-add-silent-failure.md@sha256:b166972cf016bafad5e5e76f4e5ead0cf3b258819d0b818afc2fb039a8bd19a3"},"owner_reference":"3182","content":"## Documentation contract\\n\\n### `skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/create/start.md`\\n\\n**Step 5** (currently lines 156-158) gains a failure branch:\\n\\n```markdown\\n## Step 5: Use `item_ref` from the response\\n\\nThe `backlog_add` response contains `item_ref` \u2014 use that value directly for all downstream workflows and selector parameters.\\n\\nIf the response also carries a non-empty `error` (MCP field, or the CLI JSON payload's `\\\"error\\\"` key), the backend\\nissue could not be created even though the item itself was stored: `item_ref` will be `\\\"\\\"` and `reference` is the\\nonly selector for this item until an issue is created for it. Report the error text to the user, use `reference`\\n(not `item_ref`) in Step 6's confirmation and next-step commands, and do not treat this as the generic\\n\\\"MCP tool result contains `error`\\\" stop condition in Error handling below \u2014 the item exists and Step 6 still\\napplies, just without an issue reference.\\n```\\n\\n**Completion criteria** (currently lines 187-192), first bullet needs a parenthetical\\nso it doesn't contradict the new Step 5 branch:\\n\\n```markdown\\nCreation is complete only when:\\n- `backlog_add` returns with no non-empty `errors` (a populated `error` field with GitHub-issue-creation-failure\\n  text is not itself a stop condition \u2014 see Step 5's failure branch \u2014 but any other non-empty `error`/`errors` is)\\n- `item_ref` is normalized to `#N`, or, if Step 5's failure branch applied, `reference` is used in its place\\n- confirmation is shown to the user, using whichever selector (`item_ref` or `reference`) Step 5 resolved\\n```\\n\\nNo other file in the Impact Radius's Documentation/Consumers sections needs changes \u2014\\nconfirmed no other skill/agent/hook reads `add_item`/`backlog_add`'s `item_ref` or\\n`error` fields (Impact Radius, \\\"Code \u2014 Consumers\\\").\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Post-Implementation Annotations\\n\\nAdded by context-refinement agent on 2026-09-04 (P8c3a5756/T6, quality-gate context refinement)\\n\\n### Design Refinements\\n\\n1. **Documentation contract refined beyond this spec's literal replacement text** \u2014 Step 5 / Error handling / Completion criteria in `create/start.md` needed a disambiguator this spec's verbatim text did not specify.\\n   - Original (this spec, \\\"Documentation contract\\\" section above): Step 5's replacement text describes only the \\\"stored with error\\\" branch \u2014 `error` populated, item stored, `item_ref` empty, `reference` is the selector. It is silent on what happens when `error` is populated but the item was **never** stored (the pre-existing `except BacklogError` raise path, e.g. duplicate/validation error).\\n   - Actual: commit `51823112c` (`fix(work-backlog-item): distinguish stored-with-error from never-stored in create doc`), made during the TN-verification-gate's correction pass rather than by the original T5 task, added an explicit disambiguator to Step 5, the Error-handling bullet, and Completion criteria \u2014 checking for a non-empty `reference`/`file_path`/`title` alongside `error` to distinguish \"stored with error\" (Step 5's carve-out, does not stop the workflow) from \"never stored\" (the generic stop condition, unchanged). This closes a real ambiguity the literal spec text left open, without changing this spec's design decision (only the \"creation raised\" sub-case ever populates `error` on a stored item \u2014 that decision is unaffected).\\n   - Recorded in: P8c3a5756/T6 (context-refinement); also independently observed and endorsed by the doc-drift-audit artifact (`doc-drift-audit-qg-backlog-add-silent-failure`) and reviewed/passed by the T1 code-review artifact (`code-review-T1-qg-backlog-add-silent-failure`).\n   - Classification: design-refinement (auto-record) \u2014 same goal (route the doc-consuming agent correctly across the full three-outcome-plus-never-stored space), narrower/more complete implementation than this spec's literal text, no scope or goal change. No `Intent Source` reference exists on this artifact or on the feature-context artifact (pre-policy), so intent-divergence classification does not apply \u2014 see the dh:context-refinement skill's Step 5.4.\\n\\n2. **Impact Radius \\\"one documented consumer\\\" claim was one consumer short.** This spec's Documentation contract section states \"no other skill/agent/hook reads `add_item`/`backlog_add`'s `item_ref` or `error` fields.\" A second consumer, `skills/interop/SKILL.md` (Step 3 mermaid flow, lines 87-95), branches on the mere *presence* of a non-empty `error` key and ABORTs \u2014 a contradiction structurally identical to the one this spec's Documentation contract fixed in `create/start.md`, but not itself named as in-scope. Found and verified real during T5, routed to backlog item #3400 (linked to plan Pdea64bb9) rather than fixed under this item. Not a defect in this spec's analysis method, but the underlying Impact Radius search (grep for field names) missed a consumer that branches on key-presence rather than quoting the field name near `item_ref`/`error`. Recorded in: P8c3a5756/T6; item #3182 Concerns section (entries 2026-09-04T03:43:51Z, 04:27:44Z)."}